<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Oct producer price index up 8.3 pct.</title>
<headline>S.African Oct producer price index up 8.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's all-commodities producer price index rose 1.3 percent in October from September after rising 0.4 percent in September, Central Statistical Service figures show.</p>
<p>The year-on-year rise in October was 8.3 percent after September's 7.6 percent rise.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast PPI would rise 1.0 percent month-on-month and 7.9 percent year-on-year.  </p>
<p>    Pct changes:	     Year/year		    month/month</p>
<p>			 Oct '96   Sep '96   Oct '95  - latest   prev</p>
<p>All commodities    8.3	 7.6	 8.2	   1.3	0.4</p>
<p>Locally produced   8.5	 8.6	 8.8	   0.8	0.4</p>
<p>Imported	     7.7	 4.7	 6.7	   3.0	0.1</p>
<p>Index (base 1995=100):</p>
<p>			 Oct '96   Sep '96   Oct '95</p>
<p>All commodities    109.8     108.4     101.4</p>
<p>Locally produced   110.5     109.6     101.8</p>
<p>Imported	     108.0     104.9     100.3</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
